i'm just like what  i wasn't even really offended i was just  shocked  that somebody could say something so  blatantly ignorant and racist and  unprofessional  hey guys welcome back to the channel if  you're new here my name is dani  and i'm a licensed architect in  beautiful vancouver bc so  this happened to me a few years ago at  my very first architecture job here in  vancouver  and so we were designing these offices  for  a municipal client but  everything was very very very  new for me um i didn't really know what  i was doing  and i made a lot of mistakes and i had  imposter syndrome  and i was generally just very insecure  about my abilities  anyways for this project we were  specifying  a ceiling product and i won't say what  exactly that product is because it might  expose this individual  so uh typically when we specify products  we  call the manufacturer and  the rep from that company will give you  some of the information about the  product and so there was this one  particular rep  that was helping me and uh honestly  like every time we were talking he was a  little  like tmi you know just a little bit too  much  personal information that i didn't  really need to know you know here  um at least here in the west coast um  we do a lot of small talk so you know  you start off the conversation with like  how's it going  how's your day oh it's like raining cats  and dogs here  i hope you're staying dry and  you know you try to build rapport with  this person before you  jump into business and um  like every single time he would just  dive a little bit  too far into his personal details  and um so i thought that was kind of  weird  and so one day he came over to the  office to  show me a bunch of their samples and  even before he got to our office he  called and he was like  oh i'm stopping by this office this  office this office  and oh yeah like they all love me there  so um yeah i'm just trying to paint you  a  image of this person and so  he like finally got to our office and of  course  this was the first time that we were  meeting like face to face  and he was like this big white dude  and his energy was kind of off  and he was kind of just like standing  there and i was like  hi i'm danny  and you know typically when the rep  comes they're like super friendly they  shake your hand  and like he didn't really reach out for  a handshake  this was before copen and so i was like  oh hey  i'm demi and you know whatever  so we sat down at the table and you know  it was just me and him  and he was showing me their product  and the whole time he was like making it  seem like  he was doing me a huge favor like  oh don't worry you can keep all these  samples and brochures  and i'm like no we're okay like we don't  have enough space in the office  and he was like no no no i insist you  can keep it i have plenty  so at first  i don't know that was kind of annoying  because i wasn't saying no  just to be polite like we literally were  actively trying not to  hoard materials in the office because we  didn't have enough space  and so we went through all the materials  and i asked him a bunch of questions  about the materials and  he kept saying things like oh yo like  i'm here for the weekend  um he was from calgary and he was like  oh my schedule is all  free if you wanna show me around  and um of course like at that point i  kind of knew he was  trying to hit on me and so  i'm just you know trying to like get  this person out the door  and he keeps going like oh yeah like we  have  tons of different types of samples in  our head office in calgary  like if you ever come visit i can show  you around and i can show you around the  city  and so i was like no i think i'm  good for now and so i was like okay well  thank you so much for coming all the way  here that was really helpful  and um i think i got all the information  i need  and i think i have a meeting now so um  you know just like trying to keep it  professional  and so um i got up  and i'm like ushering him out the door  and and he's like  wait wait wait  i'm like okay oh god what's he gonna say  next  and he like looks at me and he pauses  and he's like wait wait i gotta ask  what kind of asian are you  i'm just like what  and like before i can even answer he's  like  [Music]  and i i just kind of laughed i was like  okay thanks bye so  um so i closed the door  and i was just like flabbergasted that  this  even happened like i was i wasn't even  really offended i was just  shocked that somebody could say  something so  blatantly ignorant and racist and  unprofessional  but i think i was just more upset  about like wondering um like should i  have said something  how should i have dealt with that  situation like oh my god what's wrong  with me  um like how can i be taken seriously as  an architect if i  don't even know what to do in a  situation like this  um and so i was kind of like standing  there just like  running that scenario over and over in  my head  and i turn around  and i see my co-worker and she's like  laughing her head off  and um i think in that moment i just  realized that  like my head was so wrapped around  me and like what i should have done  because i was so insecure to see that  um i was starting to turn  the problem into me when it was like  obviously  this person who was the problem and i  was just like so  wrapped up in myself to see that this  was like an objectively  kind of funny situation and so i  started laughing and we just both  like sit there and laugh for like a good  five minutes  and you know she was this new senior  architect  and she was someone that i really  admired and like we  never really had the time to bond so  that was like  in a weird way kind of a nice bonding  experience  and so what i also realized  then is that you know it's not really  worth  me getting mad about you know we can  just decide to never use that company  like  this guy this company  just lost a multi-million dollar project  and like all of our future business  and i will not recommend this company to  anyone i work with  um and i think someone who is like  ignorant and unprofessional and  objectifies women  they're eventually gonna get weeded out  as  more and more women and more minorities  move into  like decision making positions that  being said  i do want to be a good role model and  like help  improve the industry for all the young  women coming into it  so maybe like the better way for me have  been  to like sit him down and explain to him  that it's not appropriate to talk like  that  and you know maybe if this had happened  to me now  um i would have done that because i have  a little bit more  self-worth and like less patience for  things like this  but the reason i'm telling you the story  now is because  well first of all i think it's kind of  funny and  because i think sometimes like we can  get really wrapped up in our own heads  and our own insecurities to really  see things clearly and you know this is  not the only instance when  like i have somehow found a way to beat  myself up about  a situation that was like obviously not  my fault  and now i'm just trying to be a little  bit more conscious  of that little subconscious  self-doubting part of my mind  and try to catch it whenever it starts  to creep in  so i would encourage you guys  to try doing the same if you have the  same problem  like monitor your thoughts and  you know try to look at the scenario  objectively  if you have the opposite problem where  you're always blaming other people  that's another problem of its own  so if you enjoyed the story remember to  hit that like button  and let me know in the comments if  you've ever been  in a situation like this we will return  to our regular programming next week  but in the meanwhile if you're looking  for some  actually valuable videos check out my  videos  like how to present case studies or  some of my architecture projects i'll  see you guys next time  bye new dude  you

